Author:     Mel Gorman <mgorman@techsingularity.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Feb 2 20:10:53 2016 +0000
Commit:     Mel Gorman <mgorman@techsingularity.net>
CommitDate: Wed Feb 17 18:14:41 2016 +0000

    mm, vmscan: Simplify the logic deciding whether kswapd sleeps
    =

    kswapd goes through some complex steps trying to figure out if it
    should stay awake based on the classzone_idx and the requested order.
    It is unnecessarily complex and passes in an invalid classzone_idx to
    balance_pgdat().  What matters most of all is whether a larger order has
    been requsted and whether kswapd successfully reclaimed at the previous
    order. This patch irons out the logic to check just that and the end re=
sult
    is less headache inducing.
    =

    Signed-off-by: Mel Gorman <mgorman@techsingularity.net>

